__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"CAMPAIGN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return n}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"chapterById",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return s}});var t=r(d[0]);const o=(t,o,n,s,l,h,c,u,p)=>({id:t,name:o,description:n,businessValue:s,feasibility:l,readiness:h,dependsOn:c,cost:u,raises:p}),n=[{id:1,title:'The Mandate',setting:`${(0,t.co)()} headquarters, boardroom. Bad coffee and nervous energy.`,opening:'Thomas played the Hemvik demo: a customer describes her room, and seconds later it appears, fully furnished. Conversion tripled. Average order value up forty percent. Built in twelve weeks. Then he looked at you. "Make us AI-first."',lesson:'You cannot plan against a number you invented. Before anything else, find out where you actually stand.',goal:{kind:'assess',count:3},goalText:'Assess at least three dimensions before committing to anything.',initiatives:[o('catalogue','Unify the product catalogue','Boring. Unglamorous. Everything else depends on it.',3,4,4,['processes'],2,{data:2,processes:1}),o('assistant','AI shopping assistant','Answer Hemvik directly. Describe a room, see it furnished.',5,3,2,['data','technology'],2,{technology:1,capabilities:1}),o('forecast','Warehouse demand forecasting','Gothenburg already runs 15% faster on one supervisor\'s intuition.',4,4,3,['data','processes'],1,{valueStreams:1,data:1})]},{id:2,title:'The Reality Check',setting:'Priya\'s small tenth-floor office, surrounded by red-inked diagrams.',opening:'Five days of scoring every dimension of AI readiness, one to five. Later Elena would say it took three. The missing two days changed everything. The number came back: 1.7.',lesson:'The gap between what leadership believes and what is true is the whole problem. Closing it costs you credibility in the short term and saves the programme in the long term.',goal:{kind:'assess',count:8},goalText:'Assess all eight dimensions. Tell Thomas the real number.',incident:{text:'Priya pulled up dashboards nobody had commissioned, databases nobody had audited, logs nobody had read.',effect:'reveal'},initiatives:[o('data-owners','Name owners for every core dataset','Nobody owns the customer record. That is why nobody can fix it.',3,4,4,['processes'],1,{data:1,operatingModel:1}),o('single-entity','The single-entity test','Pick one customer. Try to see everything you know about them.',2,5,5,[],1,{data:1,valueStreams:1})]},{id:3,title:'The Vision',setting:'A converted farmhouse forty minutes north of Stockholm. A frozen lake. A whiteboard wall.',opening:'No projector. No conference phone. Just the wall and the people. You uncapped a marker, then capped it again without writing. You do not need forty slides. You need a framework, and a provocation.',lesson:'Strategy is choosing what not to do. Every shift you commit to costs someone something, and pretending otherwise is how programmes die quietly.',goal:{kind:'trust',who:'jonas',atLeast:45},goalText:'Leave the offsite with Jonas at 45+ trust. He decides whether your team commits.',initiatives:[o('six-shifts','Commit to the Six Shifts','Commands to conversations, through to a hybrid workforce. Publicly.',4,3,3,['operatingModel'],1,{operatingModel:1,culture:1}),o('capability-map',`Map what ${(0,t.co)()} actually does`,'Capabilities, not applications. Most leaders cannot list them.',3,4,4,[],1,{capabilities:2})]},{id:4,title:'First Blood',setting:'The Fjorden whiteboard, 7:45 Monday. Six shifts. Five phases. Twelve months. 1.7.',opening:'You drew a vertical line. Left: KNOW. Right: BUILD. Jonas arrived with a binder and the expression of a man who had spent the weekend with opinions.',lesson:'The first thing you ship teaches the organisation what this programme is. Choose the boring one that works over the impressive one that fails.',goal:{kind:'ship',count:1},goalText:'Ship one capability that survives contact with production.',initiatives:[o('returns','Returns prediction model','Unglamorous, measurable, and it holds through an assortment change.',4,4,4,['data'],2,{data:1,valueStreams:1,capabilities:1}),o('bigbang','Full customer AI across all channels','Marcus wants the headline. It is not ready and neither are you.',5,2,1,['data','technology','processes'],3,{capabilities:2})]},{id:5,title:'The Resistance',setting:'Two months in. The six-week board update went better than expected.',opening:'Returns model in production, holding at 94% through the spring assortment change \u2014 the correction queue Ingrid\'s team feeds it every week is the reason it holds. Then adoption stopped climbing. Three sources: technical resistance, human resistance, governance gaps.',lesson:'Adoption is not a technology problem. A model nobody uses is worth exactly nothing, and the people refusing it usually have a reason.',goal:{kind:'adoption',atLeast:35},goalText:'Get adoption above 35%. Shipping is not the same as being used.',incident:{text:'Three sources of resistance surface at once: technical, human, and governance gaps.',effect:'none'},initiatives:[o('correction-queue','Fund the correction queue','Ingrid\'s team feeds the model weekly. That is why it holds at 94%.',3,5,4,['processes'],1,{processes:1,data:1}),o('consult-unions','Consult the unions before the rollout','Katrine keeps notes. Tell her before she reads it in an announcement.',2,5,4,[],1,{culture:2}),o('force-adoption','Mandate usage from the top','Faster. Thomas would back it. Katrine would never forgive it.',3,5,2,['culture'],1,{culture:-1})]},{id:6,title:'The Rollout',setting:'Month four. The customer service centre. Sixty-three people working at human speed.',opening:'You watched Astrid open an email about a delayed delivery. Copy the order number. Switch to the ERP. Search. Find the shipment reference. Switch to the shipping portal. Wait. Read the tracking. Switch back. Type a response. Four minutes twenty-two. Times sixty-three people, all day.',lesson:'Scaling a pilot means scaling whatever the pilot was standing on. Scale onto chaos and you get chaos at scale.',goal:{kind:'dimension',dimension:'processes',atLeast:4},goalText:'Get Processes to 4/5 before scaling, or the rollout multiplies the mess.',initiatives:[o('service-copilot','Service desk coworker','Four minutes twenty-two, done in twenty seconds. Sixty-three people.',5,4,3,['processes','data'],2,{valueStreams:2,capabilities:1}),o('standardise','Standardise the service process first','Every agent does it differently. Automate that and you get sixty-three different mistakes.',3,4,5,[],2,{processes:2})]},{id:7,title:'The Crisis',setting:'6:47 AM on a Tuesday. Elena in the shower. The phone lighting up in a cascade.',opening:'Priya: pricing inconsistency across Nordic regions, customer-facing, escalating. Jonas: service desk flooded, Norway and Denmark showing different prices for identical products. Marcus: stores in Bergen, Trondheim and Stavanger asking why the AI is quoting numbers nobody approved.',lesson:'The gate exists for the morning you find out what it was catching. How you recover matters more than the failure.',goal:{kind:'survive',quarters:2},goalText:'Contain it and keep the room. Two quarters without losing a stakeholder.',incident:{text:'A capability shipped without the deployment gate is generating different prices per region.',effect:'crisis'},initiatives:[o('rollback','Roll back and publish the post-mortem','Jonas will respect the gate being honoured, even late.',3,5,5,[],1,{technology:1,operatingModel:1,culture:1}),o('control-plane','One enterprise control plane','Federated execution, central governance. What the architecture toolkit said in chapter three.',4,3,3,['technology'],2,{technology:2,operatingModel:1}),o('blame','Blame the vendor and move on','Fast. Thomas might buy it. Jonas will not.',1,5,2,[],1,{})]},{id:8,title:'The Turning Point',setting:'Month eight. Monday morning, walking through Stockholm headquarters.',opening:'Six months ago this floor had the oppressive energy of a call centre \u2014 queue lengths in anxious red, agents speaking in scripted cadences. Today the screens still show metrics. The numbers are different. Something changed and you cannot pinpoint when.',lesson:'You do not convert a sceptic by persuading them. You convert them by being right in public, repeatedly, where they can check your working.',goal:{kind:'trust',who:'marcus',atLeast:60},goalText:'Bring Marcus to 60+. He called it a gimmick. Show him the commercial number.',initiatives:[o('commercial-proof','Put the value model in front of the board','Five categories, frozen baseline, no invented metrics.',4,4,4,['valueStreams'],1,{operatingModel:1,culture:1}),o('conversion','Answer Hemvik on conversion','Marcus only believes conversion and average order value.',5,4,4,['data','capabilities'],2,{capabilities:1,valueStreams:1})]},{id:9,title:'The Compound',setting:'Month nine. The cross-functional intelligence layer goes live. All six shifts operating at once.',opening:'Anna walked in with a printout. A recommendation from the cross-functional AI: the Klarvik dining set trending in customer service inquiries in one region, before it showed anywhere in the sales data. Nobody asked it for that.',lesson:'The compounding gap. AI-first winners separate from AI-curious competitors not by moving faster, but because everything they build makes the next thing cheaper.',goal:{kind:'adoption',atLeast:70},goalText:'Reach 70% adoption with the operating model holding without you.',initiatives:[o('cross-functional','Cross-functional intelligence layer','The capabilities start talking to each other. Value nobody planned for.',5,4,4,['data','capabilities','operatingModel'],2,{capabilities:1,valueStreams:1,operatingModel:1}),o('handover','Make yourself unnecessary','If it needs you in the room, it is not an operating model. It is a project.',4,4,4,['operatingModel','skills'],2,{operatingModel:2,skills:1})]}],s=t=>n.find(o=>o.id===t)},923,[848]);
